  "worked_solution": "The absolute value of a positive number equals the number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∣20\\,∣\\,=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of a number gives the distance between the number and zero on a number line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14145654/assets/479a1bd306e54770c7fd87759942bdbae9dbd656a74f81a8fe628b9ca3a2a089.png)",
